\section{The Four Types of Multiplicative Transformations}
We reinterpret multiplication as a composite operation consisting of four distinct transformations:
\begin{description}
    \item[Expansion (\( \times \)):] Multiplication by numbers greater than 1, which increases magnitude.
    \item[Reduction (\( \otimes \)):] Multiplication by numbers between 0 and 1, which decreases magnitude.
    \item[Reversal (\( \oslash \)):] Multiplication by negative numbers, which reverses the sign (reflects across zero) while preserving absolute value.
    \item[Nullification (\( \perp \)):] Multiplication by 0, which nullifies or annihilates the number.
\end{description}

